    "body": "Once a BLE HID device shows up in the macOS Bluetooth device list then it should also be enumerated by WebHID, but you'll need to request permission again since the WebHID and Web Bluetooth permissions aren't connected in any way.\r\n\r\nI agree this is awkward and I don't think it helps users to track permissions on such a granular level. I think it would be better to unify permissions so users are only prompted once per physical device. Getting that right will take some careful thought since it's not always easy to identify the physical device that's exposing a particular HID interface and making a mistake can potentially allow access to more devices than the user intended.",
